1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,510
What if a token's reserves, loan rights, and repayment history were verifiable directly on near?

2
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:13,276
Floorline is a near testnet protocol that combines a reserve-backed fungible token with lender-funded borrowing.

3
00:00:13,276 --> 00:00:17,881
The backing, liabilities, and loan ownership rules live on chain.

4
00:00:17,881 --> 00:00:23,263
Floor is a N E P one forty one token with separately accounted near backing.

5
00:00:23,263 --> 00:00:28,065
L over T is an accounting ratio, not a market-price guarantee.

6
00:00:28,065 --> 00:00:33,223
Redemption uses a programmed curve with a twenty percent configured tax.

7
00:00:33,223 --> 00:00:37,302
A redemption burns floor and creates a native near claim.

8
00:00:37,302 --> 00:00:40,539
This is not just a simulated button.

9
00:00:40,539 --> 00:00:46,368
Here is the finalized withdrawal transaction and its receipt evidence on public testnet.

10
00:00:46,368 --> 00:00:49,315
A lender supplies the loan funds.

11
00:00:49,315 --> 00:00:51,842
The borrower locks floor.

12
00:00:51,842 --> 00:00:57,052
The right to repay and reclaim collateral becomes a transferable N F T.

13
00:00:57,052 --> 00:01:02,184
Here the N F T changes hands, and its new owner completes repayment.

14
00:01:02,184 --> 00:01:05,881
This is a financial entitlement, not artwork.

15
00:01:05,881 --> 00:01:13,894
If the deadline passes without repayment, the contract settles the default and allocates collateral to the lender according to its rules.

16
00:01:13,894 --> 00:01:18,763
After finishing the test, we permanently stopped new financial risk.

17
00:01:18,763 --> 00:01:22,802
Then we verified an existing user could still exit.

18
00:01:22,802 --> 00:01:26,460
Both actions have finalized public receipts.

19
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:28,605
New risk stopped.

20
00:01:28,605 --> 00:01:31,289
Post-stop exit verified.

21
00:01:31,289 --> 00:01:37,447
Forty public-testnet acceptance steps were independently reconciled across the receipt tree.

22
00:01:37,447 --> 00:01:42,407
Judges can inspect the evidence and run our read-only verification scripts.

23
00:01:42,407 --> 00:01:50,289
Floorline demonstrates verifiable lending, N F Ts that carry enforceable financial rights, and bounded safety controls.

24
00:01:50,289 --> 00:01:55,342
Its open implementation shows how these primitives can be composed on near.

25
00:01:55,342 --> 00:01:59,881
The code, evidence, and verification instructions are public.

26
00:01:59,881 --> 00:02:04,947
Floorline: programmable money with verifiable rights, built on near.

